  "narrative": "I registered refinements that follow from the current central evidence rather than retesting broad effects that are already accepted and validated. The strongest newly accepted reversal is MSI-high associated with much stronger dependency. Its broad estimate is far above threshold, but it was discovered by reversing an initially incorrect +1 direction, so it needs robustness checks before treating it as a stable dataset-specific finding. I therefore registered a clean central-background test of MSI-high among cells that are TP53-intact, KEAP1-intact, and SMARCA4-intact. For this and other stronger-dependency claims, direction -1 means that the signed estimate will be positive if the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast is negative, i.e. if the exposed group has a more negative dependency_composite and therefore stronger dependency. A positive interval wholly above +0.15 would support the MSI-high stronger-dependency claim in that background; a near-zero or lower-bound-below-threshold result would suggest context dependence or insufficient precision.  I also registered MSI-high within KEAP1-loss and SMARCA4-loss backgrounds. These are scientifically important because KEAP1 loss is associated with much weaker dependency while SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger dependency. If MSI-high remains associated with stronger dependency within KEAP1-loss, that would argue the MSI association is not an artifact of the broad KEAP1-loss pattern. If MSI-high remains associated with stronger dependency within SMARCA4-loss, that would indicate additional association beyond the already very strong SMARCA4-loss effect. These loss-background tests may have smaller exposed cells, so invalid cells or wide intervals would not prove absence; they would be treated as inconclusive unless the point estimate and interval clearly support or reject threshold behavior.  I registered an interaction of MSI-high with high mutation burden within the clean TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact background. MSI-high status is often correlated with high mutation burden, so this probe asks whether the MSI-high dependency association is broadly independent of mutation burden or concentrated in high-mutation-burden cells. The interaction direction is negative: a positive signed interaction above threshold would mean the raw MSI-high-minus-non-MSI contrast is more negative in high-mutation-burden cells than in the low-mutation-burden complement. However I set anticipated_direction to 0 because a null additive result is very plausible if MSI-high itself captures the relevant signal.  The SMARCA4-loss refinements test whether the central strong SMARCA4 effect persists inside opposing molecular backgrounds. Specifically, I registered SMARCA4 loss among KEAP1-loss cells and among TP53-loss cells. These are complements to existing accepted contexts: SMARCA4 loss has already been shown in low-mask KEAP1/STK11-intact cells and TP53-intact cells. Testing KEAP1-loss and TP53-loss backgrounds asks whether the SMARCA4-loss association is diluted, reversed, or robust when combined with markers associated with weaker dependency. Direction -1 is used because the hypothesis is that SMARCA4-loss cells have a more negative composite score than SMARCA4-intact cells within that background.  I also registered PTEN loss among TP53-intact and SMARCA4-intact cells. PTEN has already emerged as a secondary context-dependent stronger-dependency predictor, especially in TP53-intact and low-mask backgrounds. This new context excludes SMARCA4 loss but not KEAP1 loss, asking whether the PTEN signal remains when the strongest strong-dependency background is absent. Direction -1 is expected if PTEN-loss cells have stronger dependency than PTEN-intact cells in this context. If the interval remains below threshold, that would further support the conclusion that PTEN is not a first-tier broad predictor but a context-dependent secondary association.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 6 explore state: Central dataset-specific dependency map is strong: SMARCA4 loss associated with much stronger dependency; KEAP1 loss and TP53 loss associated with weaker dependency; MSI-high accepted as associated with much stronger dependency after direction reversal. PTEN is secondary context-dependent stronger-dependency signal. Broad nulls/unsupported include KRAS, STK11 main, MYC amplification, PIK3CA, ARID1A, MTAP, RB1, SMAD4, markers D/E/F, APC, NF1, BRCA2, BRAF, EGFR amp, ERBB2 amp, Avana, matched omics, media serum; KY library raw direction is below threshold opposite direction and not accepted.  New explore proposals target MSI-high robustness and remaining central-context localization. MSI_high refinements: triple-intact TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact; within KEAP1-loss; within SMARCA4-loss; interaction by high mutation burden within triple-intact background. All MSI claims direction -1 expected raw negative = MSI-high stronger dependency. SMARCA4 context refinements: within KEAP1-loss and within TP53-loss, direction -1 expected raw negative = stronger dependency. PTEN refinement: within TP53-intact and SMARCA4-intact, direction -1 expected raw negative = stronger dependency.  Analysis selection next should prioritize: (1) triple-intact MSI-high; (2) MSI-high in KEAP1-loss/SMARCA4-loss if cells valid; (3) SMARCA4 in KEAP1-loss and TP53-loss; (4) PTEN TP53/SMARCA4-intact; (5) remaining active direct claims H43 DNA omics, H68 RNA omics, H69 HUMANGE_CD, H53 CDKN2A in TP53 loss, H60 SMARCA4 in STK11 loss, H61 KEAP1 in STK11 loss. Validation capacity remains 6 new requests. Next appraise should likely request validation for H80 MSI-high broad claim if new MSI context results do not create contradictions. Do not waste validation on already validated central effects. Maintain distinction: dataset-specific associations, not causality or generalizability."
